From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cinders of Chaos <noreply@cindersofchaos.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:06:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Profile: time map panning frames (--profile-pan)

Adds an automated pan mode for timing runs. After the initial view is
ready the camera moves east, then south, at a fixed speed in tiles per
second (--profile-pan SECONDS, --profile-pan-speed N). Every presented
frame is timed on the render thread and the DME_LOAD record
map_pan_complete reports frames, fps and the avg/p50/p95/p99/worst
frame interval. Optional view setup: --profile-tile-size, --profile-floor,
--profile-lighting 0|1, --profile-animations 0|1,
--profile-lower-floors 0|1. --profile-timeout SECONDS replaces the fixed
60 s readiness limit (default unchanged). Without these options the
editor behaves as before.
